solution.explanation:
Answer D – Complications arising from SWL in children are usually self-limiting and transient. The most common are:
•renal colic;
•transient hydronephrosis;
•dermal ecchymosis;
•UTI;
•formation of Steinstrasse;
•sepsis;
•rarely, haemoptysis. In children with sterile pre-operative urine cultures, antibiotic prophylaxis to decrease infectious complications is not recommended [1013]. However, every effort should be made to sterilise the urine before performing SWL, ureteroscopy (URS), or PCNL. EAU page - 77
